sition":5,"arabic":"١","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"Say: \"I seek refuge with (Allâh) the Lord of mankind,","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[{"text":"Narrated ‘Âishah رضي الله عنها: whenever Allâh’s Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم went to bed, he used to recite Sûrat Al-Ikhlâs (112), Sûrat Al-Falaq (113) and Sûrat An-Nâs (114) and then blow on his palms and pass them over his face and those parts of his body that his hands could reach. And when he fell ill, he used to order me to do like that for him. (Sahih Al-Bukhari, Vol.7, Hadith No.644).","ref":null}],"targetKey":"114:1:4","targetGloss":"(of) mankind","targetTransliteration":"l-nāsi","sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"]},{"ref":"26:39","tokens":[{"key":"26:39:1","position":1,"arabic":"وَقِيلَ","kind":"word","gloss":"And it was said","transliteration":"waqīla","lemma":"قَالَ","root":"قول","entryId":"l-effaf24a5c86c56f"},{"key":"26:39:2","position":2,"arabic":"لِلنَّاسِ","kind":"word","gloss":"to the people","transliteration":"lilnnāsi","lemma":"نَّاس","root":"نوس","entryId":"l-490d7f2d4cbaf6d4"},{"key":"26:39:3","position":3,"arabic":"هَلْ","kind":"word","gloss":"Will","transliteration":"hal","lemma":"هَل","root":null,"entryId":"l-acd15f3532f2b613"},{"key":"26:39:4","position":4,"arabic":"أَنتُم","kind":"word","gloss":"you","transliteration":"antum","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null},{"key":"26:39:5","position":5,"arabic":"مُّجْتَمِعُونَ","kind":"word","gloss":"assemble","transliteration":"muj'tamiʿūna","lemma":"مُّجْتَمِعُون","root":"جمع","entryId":null},{"key":"26:39:6","position":6,"arabic":"٣٩","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"And it was said to the people: \"Are you (too) going to assemble?","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[],"targetKey":"26:39:2","targetGloss":"to the people","target